WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.090
Speaker 1: , David.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:08.590
Do you believe that people whose hobby is
politics actually get anything done politically?

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:13.580
This is a I want to be careful in how I talk
about this, because if I were to say people

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:18.210
who just follow politics as a as a hobby and
a source of entertainment don't get a damn

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:23.409
thing done, I think it would potentially be
disaffecting to many people.

00:00:23.409 --> 00:00:27.470
My view is that and we've done interviews
on this before and it's an important question.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.480
We've talked about it with Rachel bytecode
here and with other people.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.780
Political hobbyists don't get much done themselves.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.850
If they only remain political hobbyists.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:45.520
However, they may, number one, by sharing
information on social media, get other people

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.690
to go beyond being merely political hobbyists
and being actual political activists who get

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.000
things done.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.840
But for many people, being a political hobbyist
is the entry path into being more of an activist,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.830
someone who actually calls elected officials,
organizes, does voter registration, volunteers

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.780
for candidates, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.679
So if the question it's the devil is in how
you ask through the devil's in the details

00:01:09.679 --> 00:01:17.100
of the question, do people who never go beyond
merely following politics like entertainment,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.569
help to achieve change?

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:23.859
Very, very little, hopefully they at least
vote not all political hobbyists even vote,

00:01:23.859 --> 00:01:26.840
but to the extent that they do, voting is
important.

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:32.270
If the question is, can being a political
hobbyist lead to being someone that actually

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:38.049
does achieve change by becoming an organizer
or someone who volunteers for campaigns or

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:39.049
whatever else?

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:40.049
The answer is absolutely yes.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:43.770
And I know tons of people and many are in
our audience who started just by watching

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:50.210
shows, shows like this and other shows and
voted, but then eventually really became engaged.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.470
And I can think of people in lots of different
parts of the country where that's the case.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:02:01.700
So what is important is not to dismiss those
who are interested in politics and follow

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.810
it as a hobby, as people who can never get
anything done.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.119
It's a matter of encouraging them to get more
involved.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:11.470
And there are so many ways that that can be
done, either running for something at the

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.430
local level, volunteering for a local, state
or national election and doing phone banking

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.860
and text banking and all these different things.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.580
People who one other thing right now, the
candidate that raises more money in a race

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.760
is more likely to win.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.760
It's not 100 percent.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.500
It's not correlated at one.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:32.050
But there's a correlation between raising
more money and being able to and ultimately

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.220
winning.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:38.440
If you become a political hobbyist and you
donate money, you are also involved in a way

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.770
that materially affects outcomes.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:45.270
I wish that it wasn't the case that our political
system depended on money in that way.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.430
It's a disgusting, corrosive system that must
be changed.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.800
But if you're not only a political hobbyist,
but someone who donates to candidates that

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:55.430
you believe in, you are also having an impact.

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:56.430
And we know that.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.220
And there's a reason that raising money is
so important and such an important factor

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.890
in signaling who might actually win an election.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:09.980
So let's embrace the political hobbyists to
do more rather than writing them off as people

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:10.980
who make no difference.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.330
And the truth is, most people in my audience
are political hobbyists.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.080
Some percentage of them are more than that.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:22.360
And hopefully we can encourage that number
to grow even further.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:23.440
Let me know your thoughts.

